>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_cond_depth`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_cond_depth : int -> simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sets the side-condition depth limit of a simpset.

A conditional rewrite is not applied if its side conditions, together
with those already being solved, number more than the limit. If no limit
is set, the current value of `Cond_rewr.stack_limit` (initially 4) is
used. Rewrites with other relations, added with
`simpLib.add_relsimp`, are not limited.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val decide : Traverse.ssolver = {name = "decide", solve = K DECIDE};
>>_ val ss = simpLib.add_unsafe_solver decide boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> QCONV (simpLib.SIMP_CONV (simpLib.set_cond_depth 0 ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD]) “x MOD (x + 1)”;
>> simpLib.SIMP_CONV (simpLib.set_cond_depth 1 ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
```

